  {
   "id": 505897,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{8} + \\frac{5}{{12}}\">\\frac{3}{8} + \\frac{5}{{12}}</span> and express in lowest terms.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{8} + \\frac{5}{{12}}\"></span></p>\n<p>What is the LCM of 8 and 12?</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Number</td>\n<td>Factors</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>12</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>LCM</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\rm{LCM }} = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\times 3 = 24\"></span></p>\n<p>The LCM of 8 and 12 is 24.</p>\n<p>Rewrite both fractions with 24 as a denominator.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{3 \\times 3}}{{8 \\times 3}} + \\frac{{5 \\times 2}}{{12 \\times 2}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{9}{{24}} + \\frac{{10}}{{24}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Add the numerators now that the denominators are the same.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{19}}{{24}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{{19}}{{24}}\">\\frac{{19}}{{24}}</span>"
    }
   ],
